    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Profiles is the 1985 collaboration between Pink Floyd drummer Nick Mason and 10cc guitarist Rick Fenn, released on Harvest as Mason’s second album outside Pink Floyd. It is largely instrumental and leans toward polished, melodic rock with a glossy 1980s production, though it still carries a progressive sensibility in its extended compositions and layered instrumental interplay.\n\nThe album’s best-known moments are the two vocal tracks: “Lie for a Lie,” featuring David Gilmour and Maggie Reilly, and “Israel,” sung by Danny Peyronel. Reception has generally treated Profiles as a compact but underrated side project—less experimental than Mason’s earlier solo work, but notable for its strong musicianship, atmospheric writing, and the appeal of hearing Mason and Fenn balance rock craft with subtle, cinematic textures.",
